<title>SPAIN: Iberdrola outpaces sharply on Brazil buy.</title>
<headline>Iberdrola outpaces sharply on Brazil buy.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Spain's second-largest utility,  Iberdrola, sharply outpaced the market on Friday after news its consortium  was awarded a Brazilian utility.</p>
<p>&quot;It's clearly because of Brazil. The deal was great,&quot; said an analyst  at a Spanish bank.</p>
<p>By 1040 GMT, shares in Iberdrola were up 45 pesetas or 2.61 percent  to 1,770 pesetas. The overall index was basically flat, slipping 12.92  points or 0.08 percent to 6804.75.</p>
<p>On Thursday, an Iberdrola-led consortium won a controlling stake in  Brazilian power distributor Coelba for $1.6 billion, boosting the  Spanish utility's plans to compete in Latin America.</p>
<p>--Sharman Esarey, Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
